    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/cw/en/job/498822/agripark-casual-employment-register": {
      "title": "AgriPark Casual Employment Register",
      "description": "AgriPark Casual Employment Register Apply now Reference no: 498822 Work type: Casual Location: Wagga Wagga Categories: Sustainability What is the AgriPark Casual Employment Register? The AgriPark Casual Employment Register allows individuals to express interest in casual agricultural and farm‑based work at the University. When short‑term or seasonal work opportunities arise within AgriPark, the University reviews this register and may contact suitably skilled candidates to discuss potential casual engagements. Being on the register does not guarantee employment; however, it enables us to quickly connect with people who have relevant skills and availability when needs arise. Who should apply? We welcome expression of interest from individuals with relevant skills and experience in one or more of the following areas; General farm labour Livestock handling and animal care Biosecurity Soil sampling Cropping operations Horticulture and/ or vineyard work How Does It Work? 1. Express Your Interest Complete the online application form and provide details about your: Skills and experience Availability Preferred location (if applicable) Pay rate expectations 2. Stay on the Register Your application will remain active on the register for up to six (6) months. You may update or withdraw your application at any time if your circumstances change. 3. Potential Opportunities If a casual or temporary opportunity becomes available that matches your skills and availability, you may be contacted to discuss the role. 4. Employment Conditions Casual employees are engaged by the university in accordance with applicable industrial and statutory requirements. How to Apply If you are interested in joining the AgriPark Casual Employment Register , please apply online and complete the application form. For further information, please contact jobs@csu.edu.au Advertised: 01 Apr 2026 09:00 AM - AUS Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: 31 Oct 2026 11:00 PM - AUS Eastern Daylight Time Apply now Refer a friend Back to search results"
    },
    "https://external-jobs.csu.edu.au/cw/en/job/499173/business-manager": {
      "title": "Business Manager",
      "description": "Business Manager Apply now Reference no: 499173 Work type: Continuing - Full Time Location: Wagga Wagga Categories: Management, Professional Shape the future of sustainable Australian agriculture Lead operations for a nationally recognised low-emissions program Enjoy work-life balance with a 35-hour week and a hybrid work model The role Full Time, Continuing Level 8 - $113,948 to $128,980 pa (plus 17% superannuation) Wagga Wagga As Business Manager, you will play a critical role in advancing the growth and impact of the Cool Soil Initiative. Working closely with the Director, Principal Scientist and Project Leaders, you will drive business development, secure funding opportunities, and support the delivery of innovative projects. Through high-level project and financial management, you will establish strategic and operational frameworks that strengthen organisational performance and position the Cool Soil Initiative as a leader in sustainable agriculture. About you Demonstrated experience in business or operations management, with strong financial acumen including budget development and variance analysis Proven ability to manage competing priorities, exercise sound judgement, and support senior leaders in a complex environment Experience engaging with external partners, industry stakeholders, or government bodies Strong written communication skills, including the ability to prepare clear reports, briefings, and correspondence Familiarity with the agricultural, research, or higher education sector is highly regarded About us We are a university of the land and people of our regions. True to the character of regional Australia we have gumption, we have soul and we collaborate with others. We develop holistic, far-sighted people who help their communities grow and flourish. The Wiradjuri phrase yindyamarra winhanganha means the wisdom of respectfully knowing how to live well in a world worth living in. This phrase represents who we are at Charles 